2. Normality (2 pts): Run Shapiro-Wilk tests per cell (trt × time) and evaluate Q-Q plots.

3. Outliers (1 pt): Detect potential extreme outliers using boxplots or rstatix::identify_outliers().

4. Homogeneity of Variances (1 pt): Perform Levene’s test at each measurement occasion.

5. Homogeneity of Covariance Matrices (2 pts): Run Box’s M test on wide-format data using alpha = 0.001.

6. Sphericity (2 pts): Check Mauchly’s test for time and apply Greenhouse-Geisser corrections if violated.
